<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
Officer LaunchAgent template.

Per Spec 059 v1.1 Checkpoint 2.3 + Captain ratifications:
- KeepAlive=true (unconditional restart) + ThrottleInterval=30. Checkpoint
  2.3 originally ratified SuccessfulExit=false here (msg 2603 decision 1,
  restart on any non-zero exit only), but every officer actually running
  today (cos, comms-officer, and the two product-lane CEO plists this
  change retires) has always used unconditional KeepAlive=true instead —
  none of the live fleet has ever been deployed from this template, so that
  ratification was never exercised in practice. Retiring the two CEO plists
  in favor of THIS template (2026-07-14 product/captain-agnostic
  foundation) makes the template's policy load-bearing for the first time;
  reverted to match the always-on-24/7 behavior every real officer plist
  actually has, rather than silently rolling out an unverified change to a
  fleet-safety-critical restart policy. Reconciling the two policies is a
  separate, deliberate decision — not a side effect of a config-generation
  refactor.
- WorkingDirectory key (CTO v1.1 #2 — without this, scripts can't locate cabinet/.env)
- SoftResourceLimits NumberOfFiles=4096 (CTO v1.1 #3 — default 256 hits EMFILE under MCP load)
- EnvironmentVariables REDIS_HOST + REDIS_PORT (Spec 064 v1.1 CTO #6 — Mac portability)
- StandardOutPath/ErrorPath ~/Library/Logs/cabinet/ (Mac convention, NOT /var/log/)
- Label uses reverse-DNS bundle ID (Spec 058 v1.2 CRO F2 — TCC code-signing pairing)

Product/captain-agnostic foundation (2026-07-14): CABINET_ENV, CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
and CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR below were previously only set in
individually hand-committed per-officer plists (e.g. the two product-lane
CEO plists this change retires in favor of this template + the roster). Both
are FLEET-WIDE, officer-independent values, not per-product config, so they
belong here instead of duplicated per officer:
- CABINET_ENV=runtime (framework/env.py) gates framework/frontdoor/channel.py's
  allow_sends() — every officer needs this to send for real, not just the
  ones that happened to have a hand-copied plist.
- CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR (AUD-1 fleet rollout,
  audit 2026-07-07 #1): dedicated officer config home, isolated from the
  Captain's personal ~/.claude (no personal plugin set/auto-memory/corridor
  mandate). Computed from ${HOME} — no new envsubst variable needed.
  SECURESTORAGE set to EMPTY is deliberate: it drops Claude Code's
  per-config-dir keychain suffix so the officer shares the default
  "Claude Code-credentials" OAuth item (a fresh config home has no
  credentials of its own; duplicating the item would race refresh rotation).

Variables substituted by deploy-mac.sh via envsubst BEFORE writing to ~/Library/LaunchAgents/:
- ${USER}        — invoking user (id -un)
- ${HOME}        — user home dir
- ${OFFICER}     — officer slug (cos, cto, cpo, cro, coo)
- ${REPO_ROOT}   — path to captains-cabinet repo (default ~/work/captains-cabinet)
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.cabinet.officer.${OFFICER}</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>${REPO_ROOT}/cabinet/scripts/start-officer-mac.sh</string>
    <string>${OFFICER}</string>
  </array>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>${REPO_ROOT}</string>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>HOME</key>
    <string>${HOME}</string>
    <key>USER</key>
    <string>${USER}</string>
    <key>CABINET_EVENT_LOG_DIR</key>
    <string>${HOME}/Library/Application Support/cabinet/events</string>
    <key>REDIS_HOST</key>
    <string>localhost</string>
    <key>REDIS_PORT</key>
    <string>6379</string>
    <key>CABINET_ROOT</key>
    <string>${REPO_ROOT}</string>
    <key>CABINET_SOURCE_REPO</key>
    <string>${REPO_ROOT}</string>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/opt/homebrew/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    <key>OFFICER_NAME</key>
    <string>${OFFICER}</string>
    <key>LANG</key>
    <string>en_US.UTF-8</string>
    <key>LC_ALL</key>
    <string>en_US.UTF-8</string>
    <key>CABINET_ENV</key>
    <string>runtime</string>
    <key>CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR</key>
    <string>${HOME}/Library/Application Support/cabinet/claude-config</string>
    <key>CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR</key>
    <string></string>
  </dict>

  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>

  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>30</integer>

  <key>SoftResourceLimits</key>
  <dict>
    <key>NumberOfFiles</key>
    <integer>4096</integer>
  </dict>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>${HOME}/Library/Logs/cabinet/${OFFICER}.out.log</string>

  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>${HOME}/Library/Logs/cabinet/${OFFICER}.err.log</string>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Interactive</string>
</dict>
</plist>
